  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with Aura3D. The forest is a 400×400 ground plane plus three instanced nodes: 8,000 trunks (cylinders), 8,000 canopies (cones) and 2,000 rocks (flattened spheres). Placement comes from a seeded LCG, so the forest is the same on every load, scattered across a disc of radius 75. Per-instance HSL colours vary the trunks, canopies and rocks, and the base materials are white so the instance colours aren't applied twice. The scene has one shadow-casting directional light, a hemisphere fill, and exponential fog (`effects.fog` with mode \"exp\", density 0.004). The camera is `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate`, looking down on the whole forest. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set in a `requestAnimationFrame` after the first `onFrame` callback. Typecheck passes. I couldn't run `vite build` or open the scene in a browser here, so I haven't seen a rendered frame. That means the shadow quality, the fog look and the camera framing are untested.",
